A||N||13||pollock||New 'charged 3.4 Grand Am!||||10||
Z||000000||pollock||01-21-2000||10:20 AM||||In the new Motor Trend, there's an article about a GM concept Grand Am 3.4 with an Eaton M62 supercharger.  262 hp, 280 ft-lbs.<P>AND IT'S NOT THE TDC.  The charger is located at the rear of the block, above the transaxle.  It's driven by a pulley at the front of the block via a long shaft.  If it were possible to relocate it to the other side of the engine, I think you could stuff it in a Fiero bay.<P>Anyone know how to contact Eaton?  Is this the same one offered by that Canadian company that you have to lose your a/c for?<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||terryk||01-21-2000||11:31 AM||||No, it's not the RSM kit and this concept car will never see the light of day.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||01-21-2000||12:12 PM||||Terry... I saw the same article. Why don't you think the car will happen? Sounds like they had two prototypes; an automatic, and a 5-speed Getrag. Sounded like they didn't have to cobble it a great deal to make it work.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-21-2000||12:37 PM||||Raydar,<P>I agree with Terry.  This car will not see production.  If you are interested in neat toys do some research on John Moss.  He is the man in charge of GM's toybox.  They do all of the cars such as this.  Every year they make 10-20 production based vehicles with performance options.  They seldomly if ever get produced.  That does not say however that this technology could not be (rather difficultly) applied to our cars.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||01-21-2000||01:00 PM||||Seems like I've heard that name. I've seen a few stories about late model Rat-motored Camaros and 350 c.i. S-10's. This one just seemed a bit more practical. And, if I recall, GM was going to survey the folks that went to the auto shows, and ask if, <BR>1. the car should be produced at all, <BR>and 2. if they should use the name GTO.<BR>Maybe I've just allowed myself to be suckered in. (Same thing happened when I read a story, in 96, about a 200 HP Avenger R/T. I'm STILL waiting for *that* one...)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||01-21-2000||04:45 PM||||Eaton Compressor Division has a website with dimensions,specifications;the easiest way to get to it would be through Jackson Racing's site,or maybe Sebring Supercharger's site.<BR>Can't imagine what the TDC would be like with a huffer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||pollock||01-21-2000||05:23 PM||||I can't believe y'all don't think this car could get made.  There's nothing exotic about it.  The only thing i can think of that might stand in the way is that Pontiac already has the sc'd Gran Prixs.  <P>Anyhow, i checked out the Eaton site. Pretty informative.  A company called Magnuson does a lot of their aftermarket work.  Seemed like Magnuson is willing to work with an individual on an R&D basis for a one-off.  Costly, but cool.  Gotta be some way to cram that baby in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000007||olympic||01-21-2000||09:00 PM||||  Here's a link to one crazy @$$ guys site who put an eaton blower on a 3.4 TDC <A HREF="http://mae.wvu.edu/~mhawkins/super34.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://mae.wvu.edu/~mhawkins/super34.htm</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000008||2birds||01-21-2000||10:39 PM||||I don't think GM will build it either, but I'd love to see them prove me wrong.  They sell enough Grand Ams already, if the number I see around here is any indication.  They are pretty quick already, especially the GT with the 3.4.  It wouldn't take long before the insurance industry squashed it, too.<BR>The reason I don't think GM will build it is the competition factor.  Why can't you get a Monte SS with the SC 3.8?  Because the Grand Prix has it.  Why did they kill the Fiero as it got better?  So the Vette wouldn't lose sales.  GM already overloads each category enough, why build another?<BR>For my money, I'd rather have a 3.8 SC than a 3.4 SC.  Look at the higher torque output of the 3.8.  Torque is what makes you smile...||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||01-22-2000||02:09 AM||||Hi Raydar,<P>I just think it's one of Moss's show-off cars (I think Moss gets some cool stuff through too). The problem is, they crank them out like donuts. Few, especially the once's that have the big HP, make it out.<P>I think the Shortstar SC has a chance though.<BR>3.5L 24V DOHC Supercharged. I think it might replace the Buick 3800 SC.<P>Remember, you heard me speculate about it here without any fact first!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||01-23-2000||11:07 AM||||I have heard rumors that GM was looking for a replacement for the 3800, due to emissions considerations. The Shortstar sounds like a logical answer. Wonder if it will be as reliable, tho'. GM invents a real "turkey" engine, every so often. Remember the Vega? <BR>The early Quad-4, and the head gaskets?  Also, the LT-5, while making tons of power, was rumored to have had "many" warranty replacements. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||01-23-2000||11:09 AM||||But I'm NOT cynical. Really.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||2birds||01-23-2000||11:24 AM||||I think the shortstar is already in the Oldsmobile Intrigue (or is it the Alero?)  Car and Driver had an article on it about 6 months ago.  Sounds like a good engine, based on the northstar design, but wasn't the northstar related to the Quad Four?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cooter||01-23-2000||11:59 AM||||GM's toy chest is full things like that Grand Am. The Grand Prix GPX was one. The supercharged production GTP is kind of based on the GPX. In short, some of the features of these one of a kind cars will make it into production. Like when GM built a twin engine Citation. It had a front and rear 2.8 v6. But was down on power so the 2.8's were stroked into 3.1's. Sound familiar? There is a Caprice Classic with a BMW engine. Why? Because BMW pioneered the use of "Drive by Wire" technology on street cars and GM wanted to evaluate it. Now some GM cars feature a similiar system. Wouldn't it be nice to sneak into the storage warehouse and see what never made it into production?||||reg||1
